> After you grant Resource Access Management (RAM) user or RAM role under another Alibaba Cloud account, you must also use the Alibaba Cloud account of the RAM user or RAM role to authorize them to use the secret in the RAM console. Only then can the RAM user or RAM role use the secret. For more information, see [Custom policy examples for Key Management Service](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/480682.html), [Grant Resource Access Management (RAM) user](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/116146.html), and [Grant permissions to a RAM role](https://help.aliyun.com/document_detail/116147.html).', example='{"Version":"1","Statement": [{"Sid":"kms default secret policy","Effect":"Allow","Principal":{"RAM": ["acs:ram::119285303511****:*"]},"Action":["kms:*"],"Resource": ["*"] }] }', position='Query'),
  rotationInterval?: string(name='RotationInterval', description='The interval for automatic rotation. Valid values: 6 hours to 8,760 hours (365 days).  
The value must be in the `integer[unit]` format. `integer` specifies the time length, and `unit` specifies the time unit.  
Valid values for `unit`: d (days), h (hours), m (minutes), and s (seconds). For example, both 7d and 604,800s indicate a 7-day interval.  

> You must set this parameter only when EnableAutomaticRotation is set to true.', example='30d', position='Query'),
  secretData: string(name='SecretData', description='The secret value. The value can be up to 30,720 bytes (30 KB) in length. KMS encrypts the value by using the specified key and stores it in the initial version.

